# Upstream T3 Code base for Linguini (patch layout).
# The pin lives in .linguini/upstream.pin (repo=, tag= for a release-tag pin, commit=). We track stable
# upstream releases (vX.Y.Z tags; prereleases are skipped). This repo does not contain
# upstream's files: .linguini/assemble builds the tree from the pin, .linguini/patches (one per
# upstream file we change) and .linguini/deleted (upstream files we don't carry), plus our own
# files. To sync:
#   .linguini/bump            # try the patches on the latest stable release tag; reports clean / 3way / FAILED
#   .linguini/bump --write    # move the pin there and regenerate the patches (needs no failures)
#   .linguini/bump v0.2.0 [--write] / .linguini/bump main   # a specific tag, or a branch for a trial
#   then assemble, typecheck/test/build in .linguini/build, commit, open a PR.
# A FAILED patch: fix the file in the tree bump printed, then `.linguini/regen <that tree>`.
# Linguini does not carry upstream's GitHub automation. .github/workflows (except our
# linguini-ci.yml), .github/actions, .github/scripts, .github/triage, .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE,
# .github/pull_request_template.md, .github/VOUCHED.td, .github/TRIAGE_EXEMPTIONS.td and
# scripts/notify-discord-release.test.ts (it reads release.yml) are in .linguini/deleted, and
# .github/SECURITY.md is ours (a patch). After a bump, add new upstream files under
# .github/workflows, .github/scripts and similar automation to .linguini/deleted (delete them in the
# assembled tree, then regen) unless we want them.
# History: until 2026-10-14 this was a fork that merged upstream. The last fork merge base was
# 4d73e1d5cdd32dbfb470e9422421cc40475d5e99.
